From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fingerprint Lab <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 10:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] goodix550c: let manual-FDT contact settle before capturing

The manual fallback declares contact as soon as one FDT channel pair moves,
which is the leading edge of a finger that is still coming down, and the
capture followed that edge by roughly 80ms in every instrumented placement.
The frame therefore recorded whatever fraction of the pad had landed by then.
Measured non-contact areas on placements that reached full coverage a moment
later were 38.6%, 67.3% and 87.2%, against a 10% enrollment limit, while
placements that were already resting on the pad when the poll armed measured
0.0%.

Hold for a fixed settle window after contact is confirmed, then capture. The
window runs no command transaction, so no reply can be stranded and
cancellation is honoured directly. A finger withdrawn during the window
yields a frame the coverage gate rejects, which is what withdrawing it a
moment earlier already did.

This replaces the earlier reading of these rejections as an image-readout
defect. Both readouts were instrumented and the reference frame is clean on
every stage, so the rejected frames record real partial contact rather than a
stale or blank buffer.

---

--- a/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-scan.c
+++ b/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-scan.c
@@ -34,6 +34,14 @@
 #define GOODIX_MANUAL_FDT_CONFIRMATIONS 2
 #define GOODIX_MANUAL_FDT_LOG_RETRY_INTERVAL 50
 
+/* Contact is declared as soon as one FDT channel pair moves, which is the
+ * leading edge of a finger still coming down. The capture used to follow that
+ * edge by about 80ms, so the frame recorded whatever fraction of the pad had
+ * landed by then: measured non-contact areas of 38.6%, 67.3% and 87.2% on
+ * placements that reached full coverage a moment later. Let the pad finish
+ * loading before reading it. */
+#define GOODIX_MANUAL_FDT_DOWN_SETTLE_MS 300
+
 /* Phases that wait for the pad to settle must terminate on their own: the
  * operator is not asked for contact there, so an unstable pad would otherwise
  * poll forever without ever reporting a result. Only the finger-down wait is
@@ -65,6 +73,7 @@
   GOODIX_FINGER_WAIT_VALIDATE,
   GOODIX_FINGER_WAIT_POLL_DOWN_REQUEST,
   GOODIX_FINGER_WAIT_POLL_DOWN_VALIDATE,
+  GOODIX_FINGER_WAIT_POLL_DOWN_SETTLE,
   GOODIX_FINGER_WAIT_NUM_STATES,
 } GoodixFingerWaitState;
 
@@ -760,7 +769,9 @@
             fpi_device_report_finger_status_changes (dev,
                                                      FP_FINGER_STATUS_PRESENT,
                                                      FP_FINGER_STATUS_NEEDED);
-            fpi_ssm_mark_completed (ssm);
+            fpi_ssm_jump_to_state_delayed (ssm,
+                                           GOODIX_FINGER_WAIT_POLL_DOWN_SETTLE,
+                                           GOODIX_MANUAL_FDT_DOWN_SETTLE_MS);
             return;
           }
 
@@ -771,6 +782,18 @@
                                        GOODIX_MANUAL_FDT_POLL_DELAY_MS);
       }
       break;
+
+    case GOODIX_FINGER_WAIT_POLL_DOWN_SETTLE:
+      /* The settle window runs no transaction, so there is no reply to strand
+       * and cancellation can be honoured directly. A finger withdrawn during
+       * the window simply yields a frame the coverage gate rejects, which is
+       * the same outcome as withdrawing it a moment earlier. */
+      if (goodix_manual_fdt_check_cancelled (ssm, dev))
+        return;
+      fp_dbg ("Manual FDT contact settled for %dms; capturing",
+              GOODIX_MANUAL_FDT_DOWN_SETTLE_MS);
+      fpi_ssm_mark_completed (ssm);
+      break;
     }
 }
 

